course: dictionary
lesson: 1425
title: Carmine: a red from bugs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Carmine is a deep, bright red. You can meet it as a noun, a colour you can name, or as an adjective, a word that describes something. «The red food colour carmine is made from crushed cochineal bugs» tells you what carmine is: a colour, and a dye made from insects.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The red food colour carmine» tells you it is a colour used in food. «made from crushed cochineal bugs» tells you where it comes from. Cochineal bugs live on cactus plants, so carmine comes from a living thing, not a chemical in a factory.
explain: Carmine is used in sweets, yoghurt and lipstick, and artists use it in paint. «The Aztecs used it to dye cloth» tells you that people have used this red for hundreds of years. Because it comes from insects, people who do not eat animal products may avoid foods that list carmine.
fact: Carmine means a deep, bright red colour.
fact: Carmine is also a red dye or paint made from cochineal insects.
fact: Cochineal bugs live on cactus plants.
fact: On food labels, carmine may be called E120 or cochineal extract.
fact: Because carmine is made from crushed insects, it is not vegetarian.
exercise: «The red food colour carmine is made from crushed cochineal bugs.» What is carmine? | A sweet made from sugar | A type of blue paint | *A deep, bright red colour made from crushed insects | A kind of green cactus
exercise: Which colour is carmine? | Yellow | Green | *Red | Blue
exercise: Why is carmine not suitable for vegetarians? | It is made from sugar | *It is made from crushed insects | It is made from milk | It is made from plants
test: On some food labels carmine is written as E120. What does «E120» show? | A kind of paintbrush | *A natural red colouring | A sweet shop | A type of cactus
test: Which of these is a use of carmine? | Cooking pasta | Building walls | Making bread | *Lipstick
exam: In «She wore a carmine dress», what kind of word is carmine? | A verb | An adverb | A noun | *An adjective
